    {
      "id": "claim_184cd1fdf57d47a99ceab4462aed350d",
      "statement": "A cron wake is only routed to reminder_delivery if the store holds an active reminder matching reminder_id, user_id, and thread_id, and the wake_token compares equal via a constant-time hmac.compare_digest; otherwise it is routed to short_circuit and the cron_wake payload is cleared in either outcome.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/agent/gate.py#L45-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f19476b4a487bbb99411b5083e877489a5e0c878405487a7ac98ce7beea4b757:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_24083e56148443d492255369c7eafc57",
      "statement": "The gate skips the reminder store lookup entirely whenever the calling configuration's principal resolves to an authenticated member role, so a member-authenticated session can never produce a valid cron wake and is always routed to short_circuit for that path; only the scheduler's trusted, non-member call path can pass validation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/agent/gate.py#L45-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f19476b4a487bbb99411b5083e877489a5e0c878405487a7ac98ce7beea4b757:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ac6276b9154f474e8cb11497a79ccf56",
      "statement": "The coach graph wires review_document, reminder_delivery, short_circuit, coach_agent, and erase_my_data nodes all into a shared finalize node before END, while claim_document routes into review_document as a separate document-review subflow, and short_circuit selects a fixed emergency/injection/identifier-recall/out-of-scope response without any model call or follow-ups.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/agent/build.py#L36-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6eeb6aacf385acb2e5eb513aa7924fb1f180a888f95c9a29cefb9b6a27dd98b9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f77c73cec3134d7dac49369496aecaa0",
      "statement": "coach_agent() builds a fresh, checkpointer-free LangChain agent per turn using only safe-projected messages, deriving a server-side AgentContext(user_id, thread_id, human_msg_id) from authenticated configuration (generating a human_msg_id if missing), and its dynamic prompt reads saved profile/episodic memory only from store namespaces scoped to that authenticated user_id.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://healthcare_rag/agent/coach_agent.py#L227-L256",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26c776e4a05055f4e01f78f587e0b9633f9542ffb047a96c71533a6a94e87d9a:"
